{"type":"npc","name":"Whalefeller","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":80,"temp":0,"max":80,"details":""},"ac":{"value":30,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":15,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":40}],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["fey","thalassic"],"details":""},"level":{"value":11},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>In the depths of the ocean, the fall of the carcass of a massive creature like a whale or kraken is a momentous occasion. A single corpse can birth and sustain a thriving ecosystem. Like any area of natural splendor, these ecosystems can attract nymphs as guardians and caretakers.</p><p>And what becomes of these nymphs when the corpse finally gives all it can? Some become nymph wanderers, but others who can't let go of their attachments instead transform into whalefellers. These aquatic predators dedicate their lives to slaying the largest creatures they can find and guiding their corpses to the ocean floor. The death of their wards strips whalefellers of many of the natural powers of a nymph, but in exchange, it imbues them with a desperate and vicious bloodthirst.</p><p>When hunting animals proves insufficient, whalefellers have been known to hunt and sink entire ships full of sailors or slaughter villages of sea-dwelling creatures in the hopes that enough individual corpses might help kickstart new growth.</p><h2>That Was My White Whale</h2><p>Whalefellers have a selfish streak—if a leviathan of the deep is to be slain, they want to be the one who strikes the killing blow. There's nothing they hate more than a ship full of adventurous fools who battle sea monsters on their own. If denied a kill by the crew of a ship, a whalefeller might follow the ship for leagues, picking off crewmembers one by one as part of their twisted revenge.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 175/390/720 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Diplomacy, Lore [Ocean Depths], Nature, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, death, dexterity, energy resistant (fire, vitality), intelligence, spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.zfn5RqAdF63neqpP]{Control Water}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.WzLKjSw6hsBhuklC]{Create Water}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Y3G6Y6EDgCY0s3fq]{Hydraulic Torrent}), spiked, strength, water, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Cassandra Sawdon-Smith","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":7},"con":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":7},"wis":{"mod":7},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"wavesense (varies) 1 mile","mod":24,"senses":[{"type":"wavesense","acuity":"precise","range":120}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":18,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":24,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":23},"athletics":{"base":23},"diplomacy":{"base":21},"nature":{"base":22},"stealth":{"base":22},"survival":{"base":26}},"traits":{"value":["aquatic","fey","water"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"dHbYxUPOegI4rAS3","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/whalefeller.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Whalefeller","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/whalefeller.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribut