 can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with aquatic animals.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"uWkfJF0ItyVckSgC","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Aquatic Tracker","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The whalefeller can follow trails through the water via careful surveillance of currents, disturbed fauna, and other telltale signs obvious only to a dweller in the deep. They can use Survival to @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.actions.Item.EA5vuSgJfiHH7plD]{Track} even in aquatic environments.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"2T3MXkzaQWXNxsBG","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Wavesense","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The whalefeller's wavesense is precise out to a range of 120 feet, imprecise out to 300 feet, and vague out to 1 mile.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"kkKtzfqMTWbMXPUE","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Bone Harpoon","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>A whalefeller's bone harpoon is a part of their body. Unlike a typical harpoon, it doesn't have a visible rope or chain; instead, the whalefeller is magically connected to their harpoon and can recall it with Reclaim Harpoon. If another creature within 1 mile is holding the bone harpoon, the whalefeller can attempt to @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.actions.Item.Dt6B1slsBy8ipJu9]{Disarm} it, no matter how large the creature is. If the harpoon is ever destroyed, the whalefeller must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:30] save or be @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 2}.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"U2OKHc2zrQpntBNZ","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Colossus Hunter","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The whalefeller deals 4 additional damage with their Strikes against creatures that are Large or larger.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"strike-damage","value":4,"predicate":[{"gte":["target:size",3]}]}],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"7HXFiz90q1ED2QPj","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Dart Away","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The whalefeller is targeted with a melee or ranged attack by an attacker they can see that is currently taking persistent damage from Tear Free</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whalefeller gains a +2 status bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the attack misses, the triggering creature takes @Damage[2d6[piercing]] damage from fragments of bone left in the wound.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[{"key":"RollOption","option":"dart-away","toggleable":true},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"ac","value":2,"type":"circumstance","predicate":["dart-away"]}],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"DGPnRVmlPd75vArx","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Reclaim Harpoon","system":{"actionType":{"value":"free"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The whalefeller's harpoon is within 1 mile and is not being held by any creature</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whalefeller's bone harpoon returns to their hand.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"gduqZujiWUNIbJ52","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Tear Free","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The whalefeller's last action was a successful harpoon Strike</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whalefeller sprouts additional barbs from the harpoon before violently recalling it with Reclaim Harpoon. The target takes @Damage[2d6[persistent,bleed]] damage and takes a –10-foot status penalty to their swim Speed for as long as they are taking this persistent damage. Even once healed, the wound makes the target easier to track; the whalefeller gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Survival checks to @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.actions.Item.EA5vuSgJfiHH7plD]{Track} the target for 24 hours.</p><p>@UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.sf2e-effects.Item.dyws4H3Mfa0TLw3I]{Effect: Tear Free}</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"XjhN5CDhnsPq7xLK","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"melee","name":"Claw","effects":[],"system":{"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null},"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["agile","finesse","unarmed"]},"damageRolls":{"OmD4KJC7oA5jHOA4":{"damage":"2d8+14","damageType":"piercing","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":24},"attackEffects":{"value":[]}},"_id":"gGOHOMvsK3Sg4cG0","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}}],"effects":[],"sort":100049,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"sf2e","systemVersion":"0.0.11"}}